[03:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything to do with caching. So, the Reader\'s Digest version of what caching is is a model just like saves previous parts of the conversation instead of reprocessing it each and every time. So, for example, in the Astra pricing page, it says $10 per million input tokens, $1'

[03:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'per million cached input tokens. 10 times less expensive to use cached inputs as it is to you process the original. And yet, this is API pricing, not a direct comparison how it works on'

